                <pb facs="0716" n="628" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg628"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Scruggs to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-10-04"><hi rendition="#italic">October 4, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received October 5.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Scruggs reports that the blockade of Puerto Cabello is effected by two
                    inefficient Venezuelan steamers which are present there at intervals, and now
                    threaten to fire upon New York American steamers. He asks whether the naval
                    forces of the United States should respect such a blockade, should the steamers
                    make an attempt to enter.</p>
            </div>
